eport\\nEHA2024 gallery\\nEHA2023 report\\nEHA2023 gallery\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\nTrial membership\\nHealthcare-affiliated professional membership\\nEmeritu\"}}, {\"id\": \"l26\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-8bbee427c046d4c2d6e7b062\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/connect-network/membership-and-benefits/full-membership\", \"text\": \"Full membership\", \"source_region\": \"navigation\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 768, \"end\": 948, \"text\": \"A2024 report\\nEHA2024 gallery\\nEHA2023 report\\nEHA2023 gallery\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\nTrial membership\\nHealthcare-affiliated professional membership\\nEmeritus membership\\nJoi\"}}], \"supported_parent_doc_ids\": [], \"source_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-8bbee427c046d4c2d6e7b062\", \"title\": \"Connect & Network - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Connect & Network - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3886, \"end\": 4530, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 644}, {\"start\": 4771, \"end\": 4791, \"excerpt_start\": 645, \"excerpt_end\": 665}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Connect & Network\\nMembership\\nYoung EHA\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nMeetings\\nCongress archive\\n“You build a network with people you never imagined you would be talking to, including individuals from other countries whom you probably wouldn’t have connected with otherwise.”\\nDr Inge Govaerts, Young National Society Ambassador for Belgium\\nUZ Leuven, Belgium\\n“EHA offers the potential to be part of a community that is broader than a national society, which offers great opportunities to meet colleagues from different countries at events like the Congress.”\\nProf Anne Angelillo-Scherrer, Community Stakeholder Committee Member\\nUniversity of Bern, Switzerland\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-7ad170c3c8cf26dee84e0e4f\", \"title\": \"Specialized Working Groups - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Specialized Working Groups - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3922, \"end\": 3948, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 26}, {\"start\": 4003, \"end\": 5577, \"excerpt_start\": 27, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Specialized Working Groups\\nEHA’s Specialized Working Groups (SWGs) foster science and spread knowledge in basic, translational, and clinical research in hematology.\\nTo ensure we cover the full field of hematology and provide a research platform for all groups and researchers, we’ve established two types of SWG:\\nDisease-oriented SWGs—which cover specific topics such as leukemias and lymphomas\\nOverarching SWGs—which cover broad themes such as aging and precision medicine\\nThis model is based on the nine sections of the EHA Roadmap for European Hematology Research.\\nThere are currently 25 SWGs. You can use the filter below to view them by type.\\nHow to join an SWG\\nIf you’re interested in making new connections or sharing your expertise, you can apply to join an SWG. To do this, just follow the instructions on the main page of the relevant SWG.\\nSWG Grants\\nEHA provides financial support to small research projects initiated by our SWGs. You can find out more about his support, and discover some of the projects we’ve already supported, in the SWG Grants section.\\nEHA Lymphoma Group\\nEuropean Research Initiative on CLL (ERIC)\\nEuropean Scientific foundation for Laboratory Hemato Oncology (ESLHO)\\nOverarching Specialized Working Group on Diagnostics in Hematology\\nSpecialized Working Group on Acute Myeloid Leukemia\\nSpecialized Working Group on Adolescents and Young Adults with Hematologic Diseases (AYA)\\nSpecialized Working Group on Adult Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia\\nSpecialized Working Group on Aging and Hematology\\nSpecialized Working Group on Bleeding and Thrombosis\\nSpecialized Working Grou\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-06666aef272852e77f6e1d17\", \"title\": \"EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3894, \"end\": 3913, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 19}, {\"start\": 3968, \"end\": 4027, \"excerpt_start\": 20, \"excerpt_end\": 79}, {\"start\": 4404, \"end\": 5926, \"excerpt_start\": 80, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Research Grants\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · June 16, 2026\\nJune 16, 2026\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Research Grants are designed to support the future of hematology by helping talented junior researchers to:\\nConduct basic or translational lab-based research\\nGain valuable research and leadership experience\\nMove towards becoming group leaders\\nAdvance their careers\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nYou’re an EHA member\\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\\nYou have the support of an academic department and institute\\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\\nTypes of EHA Research Grants\\nThe three types of EHA Research Grant are the:\\nEHA Junior Research Grant, which can provide up to €150,000 for three years\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEach one of the three types of EHA Research Grant also has its own specific eligibility criteria. Please make sure you read the eligibility criteria for your grant type before you apply.\\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the sele\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-4a63fc37665d223b724eb647\", \"title\": \"Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3902, \"end\": 4532, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 630}, {\"start\": 4773, \"end\": 4793, \"excerpt_start\": 631, \"excerpt_end\": 651}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Research & Innovation\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nHemaSphere\\nGrants\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}], \"local_exploration\": {\"visited_doc_ids\": [\"web-049ec083060697f21e9e4005\", \"web-1b2e3ae206bf6a7d30e47fb6\", \"web-1e06c10fa8edbbfd5a34f082\", \"web-2681df3d0c7c018f4be24234\", \"web-cadb8bc3ab6b0c81b9da0eab\", \"web-b027569167b331c43c411500\", \"web-4a63fc37665d223b724eb647\", \"web-b34424f0bb7a7d0dc0752cfc\", \"web-06666aef272852e77f6e1d17\", \"web-7ad170c3c8cf26dee84e0e4f\", \"web-8bbee427c046d4c2d6e7b062\"], \"visited_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-049ec083060697f21e9e4005\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-1b2e3ae206bf6a7d30e47fb6\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants\", \"title\": \"Grants - The Eur