tive nature of the SWG network\\nEncourage the mutual exchange of expertise\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s211\",\"d1\",5385,5662,\"To increase diversity and support inclusion within our SWG community, we encourage proposals that involve:\\nJunior members\\nPartners from underrepresented countries\\nIn all cases, the principal investigator(s) (PIs) must be EHA members and SWG members at the time of application.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s212\",\"d1\",5662,6049,\"Individual applications are not eligible for this call, because each project must foster collaboration and help build a network within the relevant SWG. Please include other SWG members in your project. Non-SWG or non-EHA members will not be counted as collaborators for this grant.\\nAll applications should therefore be communicated internally within the relevant SWG before submission. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s213\",\"d1\",6049,6436,\"Applicants will be asked to confirm this in the application.\\nThe SWG Chair must submit the application, or be copied on the application email. This confirms that the application was presented to the group in advance. Each SWG may submit no more than 3 applications.\\nSelection\\nWinning grant applications are selected by the SWG Committee.\\nIn making its decision, the committee considers:\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s214\",\"d1\",6436,6771,\"• The scientific quality of the project\\n• The importance of the topic for further research/subsequent projects\\n• The explanation of the budget needs\\n• Cooperation and interaction within the SWG or with other SWGs\\n• Other sources of support that are already available for this project\\n• The overlap with ongoing/already funded projects\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s215\",\"d1\",6771,7125,\"• The inclusion of junior members and/or partners from underrepresented countries\\nHow to apply\\nTo apply, complete the application form below and send it to [email protected].\\nThe SWG Chair must submit the application, or they must be copied in on your a